  "review_notes": [
    "Three verbless clauses take supplied copulas: the two relative clauses put are on the preposition under rule 53, and the opening clause, which expresses no subject at all, puts there is on the predicate noun θεός under rule 68.",
    "Both τὰ πάντα phrases are analysed alike, the article taking the supplied nominal things and the adjective taking all (rules 22, 102); reading all things as the adjective's whole realization under rule 17 with the article unrepresented remains defensible."
